<h2 id="new-petition-rules-the-central-local-conflict-intensifies" class="headerLink">
    <a href="#new-petition-rules-the-central-local-conflict-intensifies" class="header-mark"></a>New Petition Rules: The Central-Local Conflict Intensifies</h2><p><img class="tw-inline" loading="lazy" src='/images/2026/信访新规-图2.jpg'   alt="New petition rules screenshot 2"  ></p>
<p>The most notable thing about the new petition (xinfang) regulations is not that the petitioning process has become more complicated, nor that traveling to Beijing to petition has become harder. It is what they reveal about the deeper shift now underway in central-local relations inside China:</p>
<p><strong>The center is institutionalizing the practice of pushing the social conflicts it cannot resolve back down onto local governments.</strong></p>]]></description></item></channel></rss>